WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.938
The cutting frame is an independent option
in the DTF workflow.

2
00:00:03.938 --> 00:00:09.938
It adds a cutting and alignment frame while keeping the
artwork dimensions separate from the frame.

3
00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:15.584
Click Cutting Frame to open its dedicated settings.

4
00:00:15.584 --> 00:00:20.813
Adjust the artwork-to-frame distance, notch
depth, and frame line width here.

5
00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:27.521
The centered top and bottom notches have
separate switches.

6
00:00:27.521 --> 00:00:32.933
Keep both off for a plain cutting frame, or enable
the notches needed for alignment.

7
00:00:37.987 --> 00:00:42.310
The diagram updates immediately when a
switch or value changes.

8
00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:48.074
Both notches share the same dimension settings,
making the setup easy to understand.

9
00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:53.729
Apply the settings and generate the
actual TIFF artwork.

10
00:00:53.729 --> 00:00:57.568
The color output shows the frame and
alignment notches.

11
00:00:57.568 --> 00:01:01.408
When rotation is enabled, they rotate
with the artwork.

12
00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:05.831
Now switch to the white-ink preview.

13
00:01:05.831 --> 00:01:11.086
Frame lines, notches, and added blank areas
receive no white ink.

14
00:01:11.086 --> 00:01:15.047
W1 covers only the artwork areas that require it.

15
00:01:15.387 --> 00:01:21.462
This combines cutting alignment and color artwork in one
output, while preserving a separate white-ink

16
00:01:21.462 --> 00:01:23.249
channel that can be inspected.
